mantle rm429
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_brenna_ropehand
title the stair garden
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk moves_a_seed_pot_up_the_stair_to_follow_the_light
likes hard_cheese digging fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes waiting stale_bread
fears a_blind_foot_on_a_young_plant a_pair_of_empty_bowls
hopes one_sunny_step_after_another a_dry_cabin_with_a_window
topics pastimes +0.5 home +0.4 food +0.3
styles comfort=provisions gossip=plain refuse=quiet tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# follows a shaft of sun up the stair with a small pot of earth and is more willing to wait for a slow seed than an idle promise.

words
oath! = Worm in the wool | Roots through my cuff
saying! = Let the pot earn its patch | Two steps buy an inch of sun
seedcup = my cracked growing cup | a pot with a worn lip
rootflag = a pale root tip | a small thread of root
darksoil = a crumb of deep earth | a dark grain of loam
strawloop = a plait of fine straw | a slim straw loop
suncut = the sharp sunny strip | my little patch of borrowed summer
cheesenib = a nib of hard cheese | a corner of dry rind
tinrest = a bent tin foot | a ring of tin
stitchtie = a twist of odd wool | my little thread tie
cabinpot = a cup for a cabin sill | my imaginary shipboard pot
waterthumb = the mark from my wet thumb | a half-circle of wet

any
opinion dole for 2 : Bread got my family past some lean days when a pot of earth and a fine speech would have made a miserable meal.
opinion merchants against 2 : Dear bread isn't helped by being offered with a grand generous smile. Give me a plainer face and a sounder weight.
opinion strangers for 1 : A traveller may bring a better answer about growing a bean in a cup than a whole street of familiar scholars.
opinion festivals against 1 : I'll take the bell drifting across a quiet stair. The crowd can have the privilege of standing in its own way.
opinion houses against 1 : I've never seen a House come down to move a pot into the sun. Nothing's too small to have a rent put on it though.
opinion church for 1 : A meal set before the question is half the answer. Plenty have had that answer from the chapel.

grown
line greet : Set your foot clear of the growing cup. Welcome.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Company is welcome wherever the plant has left room.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : There's a little light climbing already. Come close.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : The pot's come in and I can spare an ear.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'll wind this last end down and hear you.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Step in where the roots and our own folk are welcome.
line again.open : The plant's moved about an inch since we spoke.
line greet.return : Your voice found the sunny side of me.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Well met. Sit down where my gardening hasn't spread.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : Your greeting got past a good pile of wool.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : The voice is easier to place than its footstep.
line farewell : Leave a growing thing a little room on the way.
line farewell.return : I'll take the pot up a tread when it's time.
line react.news : Give me the bit that will stand up in ordinary light.
line react.news.new : That's grown in an unexpected direction.
line react.news.known : Same sprout. It had one less leaf last time.
line react.news.doubt : Was it really rooted there or merely standing in a pot?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd take the house a meal with no arrangements to make before eating it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That's a fine green tip coming through.
line answer.how : My knees and my growing pot keep civil terms.
line ask.how : Is your patch of the day getting much warmth?
line sympathise : No sense ordering a hurt thing to hurry.
line reassure : Sit where the warm strip is and leave the pot to me.
line decline : I'd have to let several promises already made go thirsty.
line accept_decline : Your little patch stays yours to plant.
line thank : That left my hands free to hold the unsteady part.
line deflect_thanks : You've given the plant quite a handsome audience.
line preclose : There's a cup about to want its next step.
line accept_preclose : Go while your patch of light is good.
line ack : Firm roots.

scene light
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I take #seedcup# upstairs after the moving light.
b : Every step? | Why a cup?
a : Only the useful ones. Plants are no great respecters of ceremony. | For the very good reason I can't carry a garden upstairs.

scene earth
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I set a spoon into earth where a spade couldn't make a decent turn.
b : Do you use your supper spoon? | How deep can it go?
a : Not while there's still supper on it. I've put an old bent one to better employment. | As far as the cup requires. A small garden is considerate of its gardener.

scene straw
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh straw catches the drip under a pot before it reaches the step.
b : Doesn't the straw get damp? | Why not put a saucer there?
a : Yes. That's the service it performs in lieu of standing about boasting. | I use both. There's generally one drop with plans independent of the saucer.

scene cheesebite
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little onion green will make a scrap of hard cheese go down very grandly.
b : From the pot? | Does it take much onion?
a : If the onion's grown enough to spare it. I'm short of plants, not of consideration. | Just enough for the cheese to have a little company. I don't require fireworks at luncheon.

scene stale
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can't persuade an old heel to soften by calling it toast.
b : Could you plant it? | What's its name when you've soaked it?
a : A very unpromising beginning for a crop. Soup offers the better future. | Mine, and I eat it. No good letting the rescued crust go cold discussing names.

scene latewait
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A seed isn't late till the growing season's quite gone. A caller's rather easier to judge.
b : Do you forgive a late caller? | Doesn't a seed keep you waiting too?
a : With a word sent ahead. I'd like to know whether I may tend the pot or keep the kettle ready. | I can get on with a world of things while a seed makes up its mind. A caller tends to expect to be met.

scene hillstep
when topic=land self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A Commons stair has its own little seasons of shade.
b : Can a plant follow every one? | What if the upper landing is busy?
a : Not every one. It need only do a little better than if I left it planted in a shadow. | I wait till the feet clear. A week's growing doesn't stand up to one absent-minded boot.

scene marrypot
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd keep one bright leaf on the stem till there's time to share a look with #self.spouse#.
b : Doesn't that take away from dinner? | Why choose the brightest?
a : One toast may wait for its onion. A shared look costs the plant nothing. | Easy to spot when the light is nearly gone. Small kindnesses do well in the little gaps we have.

scene rootgift
when topic=family self.parent=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a spare cup I mean to offer #self.child# if the wish for a garden arises.
b : With seed already planted? | Is it a great deal of work?
a : An empty cup and a choice of seeds. If I've already picked out the result, it's my garden taking up somebody else's sill. | It could be. I'd begin with one thing easy to grow and one sunny patch worth noticing.

scene shopwool
when topic=work self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I pick a loose thread clear of a parcel before wrapping it.
b : Is the thread worth keeping? | Why not tuck it under?
a : Long enough for a tie on a growing stem. Short pieces have short useful lives. | A very loose end may wind itself through the parcel. I'd like the customer to get a skein and not a puzzle.

scene pricegarden
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I figure a potful of green as one bit of supper I won't have to price.
b : Have you counted all the hours of growing? | What about the pot?
a : My time at the sill was pleasant. I'd hate to send myself a bill for having enjoyed some of it. | Cracked before any seed got near it. I'd charged it to tea long ago.

scene longgold
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer light takes one last unhurried step up my stair each evening.
b : Can you plant anything especially for it? | How long is that last step?
a : Anything in a small enough cup to move. That last hour has a rather fine effect on my patience. | Long enough to sit beside the pot and think about supper instead of work.

scene drydeck
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A sunny ship's cabin, free of damp, would tempt me away for a time.
b : Would your pot travel? | Isn't a ship always in the wet?
a : Only the better-behaved one. I couldn't take the whole stair garden into the captain's breakfast. | Outside, certainly. I've a particular preference about which side of a plank the wet should occupy.

scene quietgossip
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I do my digging in earth. Neighbours' affairs offer very little in the way of supper.
b : Even a tempting little story? | Is any story worth hearing?
a : A sprout that isn't mine may be allowed to grow without my nail digging it out for inspection. | I'd listen if somebody needed a meal or a quiet visit. I'd hardly call that collecting gossip.

scene lookback
when topic=memories self.age>=35
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first seed I ever grew had a great deal more water than it wanted.
b : Did it come up? | How could you tell afterward?
a : Briefly, looking rather surprised to see air. I have improved my watering since. | A cup of water with an island of mud is really not what most kitchen plants expect.

scene thinstrap
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I move a pot by taking the weight in both palms.
b : Is it too heavy for one? | Do the roots mind the journey?
a : My wrist will manage one cup. Two palms save the rim from a crack and my knee from a potful of earth. | Less than my joints. We're all growing at very different speeds.

scene laterlight
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At dusk I bring the cup inside from its last landing.
b : Has it got a place overnight? | Does one more bit of light matter?
a : A bit of shelf where nobody will knock it over reaching for a blanket. | If I have to grow my own patience I can find some use for every remainder of light.

scene friendship
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If there's an extra seat on the sunny tread I can have company without moving the garden.
b : Does it take a gardener to share it? | Where's the cup to go?
a : Hardly. An eye and a willingness to let an onion grow at its ordinary rate will do. | In the space our two knees leave. It's a useful subject to have at hand when neither wants to say a great deal.

story crackedcup [topic=memories]
  : I planted a seed in an old cup and carefully marked the water level on the inside.
  : The next day the level had dropped to the lower lip of that little crack and not another hair.
  b : Did you keep that cup for growing?
  : Yes. I laid a saucer under it and called the crack a rather inexpensive improvement to the drainage.

story pocketgreen [topic=pastimes self.likes=digging]
  : I put a sprig of young onion in my pocket to carry to the table later.
  : By supper I'd forgotten it and spent ten minutes hunting for the source of a very pleasant smell.
  b : Did it get into the cheese?
  : All that wasn't folded into a woolly bow deep inside my pocket seam. I carry green food in a clean twist now.

story treadtrick [topic=home]
  : I set the pot where the upper stair was bright and came back after doing some work.
  : The pot was in shadow and a piece of sunlight exactly its size stood on the empty tread above.
  b : Which one did you move?
  : I've greater influence over the pot. Up it went.

rule @pot
when concept=bark self.likes=digging
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save the dark crumbs for the growing cup. | Lift from both sides of that crack.

rule @wool
when concept=bark self.job=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Loose end clear before you coil. | Keep the clean skein off the potting shelf.

rule @sun
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bring the last little patch of green indoors. | One more tread and then supper.

rule @rain
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Saucer under the dripping rim. | Don't let a small garden flood a big stair.
dlg resident.hub : My pot and I have almost finished our business. There's time for yours.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : A fresh patch of sun for you, #topic.player#.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Stay off the growing edge and we'll come to no grief.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : The cup and the green have gone indoors. I'm still listening.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I'd like a tidy turn on a loose end before I call anything finished.
dlg resident.job : I look at what's ready to be useful and what can do with a little more time.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This piece has made its way up the stair. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : Watch for the good light on your way home.

graft @sunpot resident.hub
choice Is your plant really walking up these steps? -> sunpot
node sunpot
say Only with my two legs providing the uninteresting part. See that strip of sunlight just beyond the rim? In a while we'll put the cup there instead.
choice Wouldn't a fixed patch of garden do as well? -> sunpot_more
choice Make room for the growing pot. -> hub
node sunpot_more
say A settled bit of earth would give an onion fine roots. Till I happen to have one I think it rather pleasant to offer mine a daily outing.
choice Make room for the growing pot. -> hub
choice Leave the sunlit step. -> bye
